# Trempel hub — actions for a kit without its own

A kit older than 2.4 ships no `hub/actions.mdz`: the hub stands in with the project's npm scripts,
so an old project still gets its dev server, builds and gates (each only if the script exists).
A newer kit replaces this whole layer with its own.

## actions

### dev
$title: Dev server
$icon: play
$group: run
$pin: true
$kind: service
$port: auto
$when: script:dev
$shell: npm run dev -- --port ${port} --strictPort

### build:web
$title: Build (web)
$icon: package
$group: build
$when: script:build:web
$shell: npm run build:web

### build:yt
$title: Build (YouTube Playables) + gates
$icon: package
$group: gates
$when: script:build:yt
$shell: npm run build:yt

### test
$title: Unit tests
$icon: check
$group: gates
$when: script:test
$shell: npm test

### e2e
$title: e2e
$icon: check
$group: gates
$when: script:test:e2e
$shell: npm run test:e2e

### editor
$title: Scene editor
$icon: edit
$group: run
$kind: service
$port: auto
$input.folder: { type: "text", default: "scenes", label: "Scenes folder" }
$when: file:${pkg:@trempel/scene}/edit/cli.mjs
$shell: node ${pkg:@trempel/scene}/edit/cli.mjs ${input.folder} --port ${port}
